  "sourceReview": [
    "Spec: append reuses sufficient capacity; map indexes are not addressable; iteration deletion/insertion rules; clear added in 1.21.",
    "Go 1.17 map: hashGrow chooses doubling or same-size growth; growWork evacuates bucket chains, not a fixed CPU-time quantum.",
    "Go 1.17 slice threshold 1024 differs from nextslicecap threshold 256 in both 1.25.0 and 1.26.1; requested length and allocation rounding matter.",
    "Both table125.go and table126.go have pruneTombstones before growth. It is not a new Go 1.26 feature.",
    "Map Clear keeps table/directory storage; Delete clears pointer-bearing key/value references. Payload reclamation is different from table shrink and RSS.",
    "Portable matchH2 has several operations and can return extra candidates; amd64 intrinsic does not make full lookup one cycle. Always compare actual keys.",
    "Quadratic probe sequence; grow up to maxTableCapacity=1024 slots, then split; installTableSplit can grow the directory. No constant worst-case insertion promise.",
    "SwissMap flag exists in 1.25.0 flags.go and is absent in 1.26.1. Historical noswissmap must not be recommended universally.",
    "Teaching group uses occupied and empty slots. The follow-up replaces all empties with deleted; it does not invent an ordinary mixed empty/deleted group."
  ],
